--- body ---
## Context

The reading lane of M2 rests on two local readers from different model
families and a hosted arbiter, each calibrated on held-out reference answers
before any unattended run. No ticket carried this. Normative text, accepted
specification v1 (tag `jetp-spec-v1`):

- `docs/jetp-operation.md` § 5: one model per GPU (RTX A4000 16 GB, RTX 3060
  12 GB), two families, selection and calibration on OpenRouter before
  installation, re-scoring of the installed pair, what counts as a new method
  version, where each role runs.
- `docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 6.3, items "Calibration and judgement rule",
  "Reference answers, the only human check" and "Replacement readers"; § 12
  (planted-item control); § 14 (acceptance level, default "likely or more").
- `docs/jetp-requirements.md` Q5 and Q17.

Blocked by [[1509]]: selection scores candidate models by running the
reading protocol of § 6.3 on the tuning part, so the protocol must exist.
The selection run is paid and runs under the budgets of [[1874]].

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The reference answers (the cross-vendor panel reference set of [[1895]], lines made by a blind panel distinct from the readers and the arbiter, named as panel agreement) are listed and split once, by a recorded seed, into a tuning part and a held-out part stratified by language and statement shape; the held-out part is frozen with the method version
- [ ] Candidate open-weight models that fit each card are selected on OpenRouter on the tuning part only; a candidate that fails its positive controls is weighted out; the winning pair is of two makers (operation § 5, "Vendor means LLM family")
- [ ] The pair is installed on padme (exact weights, quantisation, context, sampling, template and serving software recorded) and scored again on the held-out part, with the arbiter scored on the items the readers escalate
- [ ] Each calibration record gives, per model and per stratum, the observed precision of each likelihood term with its Wilson interval, the calibration error, the recall, the end-to-end precision and the agree-but-wrong rate; strata under 30 held-out items are reported uninformative and run under the fallback of extraction § 6.3
- [ ] The acceptance level of extraction § 14 is declared for the method version
- [ ] Pilot on a stratified sample of the tuning part (language × statement shape, size stated) passes a quality check by a cross-model checker before the full selection run; findings recorded here (pilot rule, [[1500]])
- [ ] Selection and calibration spend is within the selection budget of operation § 7.2
- [ ] `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass
